Here is the code to reproduce this issue:
```java
public class TestWithCustomClassLoader {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    // Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(new MyClassLoader());
    MyClass mock = org.mockito.Mockito.mock(MyClass.class);
    System.out.println(mock.m1());
    System.out.println(mock.m2());
    System.out.println(mock.m3());
    System.out.println(mock.m4());
    System.out.println(mock.fm1());
    System.out.println(mock.fm2());
    System.out.println(mock.fm3());
    System.out.println(mock.fm4());
  }

  public static class MyClassLoader extends ClassLoader {
  }

  public static class MyClass {
    public Object m1() {
      return 1;
    }

    Object m2() {
      return 2;
    }

    protected Object m3() {
      return 3;
    }

    private Object m4() {
      return 4;
    }

    public final Object fm1() {
      return 11;
    }

    final Object fm2() {
      return 22;
    }

    protected final Object fm3() {
      return 33;
    }

    private final Object fm4() {
      return 44;
    }
  }
}
```
When I ran this code as is I get the following expected output:
```
null
null
null
4
11
22
33
44
```
However when the line `// Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(new MyClassLoader());` is uncommented it produces the following results:
```
null
2  <--- package-private method was NOT MOCKED
null
4
11
22
33
44
```
This seems to not work in Mockito 1.x and 2.x. Is this by design or a bug?

